WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.874
ALEXIS MOUSSINE-POUCHKINE:
Understanding cost

00:00:01.874 --> 00:00:04.354
can be intimidating when
trying out a cloud provider.

00:00:04.354 --> 00:00:06.270
And you may not be willing
to spend money just

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.800
to try things out.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.980
In this video, we'll talk
about Google Cloud Platform's

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.615
free trial, and the
Always Free tier,

00:00:13.615 --> 00:00:15.240
and why you should
not confuse the two.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.750
Let's start with a free trial.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.400
When you get
started with GCP, we

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.270
suggest that you sign up
for the $300 free credits.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.970
This will require you to
create an account, if you don't

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:35.180
already have a Google account,
and to provide credit card

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.830
or bank account details.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:40.610
The trial is free, and your
credit card will not be billed.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.260
You will receive
billing statements

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.090
at the beginning
of each month that

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.490
detail how much
of the $300 credit

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.890
you spent in the previous month.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:51.380
This gives you early
data points to understand

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.900
how much your future
service will end up

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.940
costing when running on GCP.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.400
And it helps you see where
you're consuming the most.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.490
You can also practice
budget management

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.209
by setting budget alerts
on your billing account

00:01:04.209 --> 00:01:07.470
or on a specific project
that you're working on.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.090
Keep in mind, these are alerts,
not limits, so pay attention

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.730
to where they notify
so you can take action

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.000
if costs ramp out of control.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.890
Once enrolled in
the free trial, you

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.920
will be able to spend the
credits on the entire platform

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.780
for any location.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.230
You are using the real stuff,
not some sandbox environment.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.650
You are, however, not able
to request quote increases,

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.810
and you cannot mine
cryptocurrencies.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:33.830
Sorry.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:35.750
Things you should
try out include

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.730
starting your first
virtual machine,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.910
transferring some data
to cloud storage buckets,

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.640
creating your first
Kubernetes Engine cluster,

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.780
running your Hadoop or Spark
workload on Cloud Dataproc,

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.030
or even training your own
machine learning model

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.070
using Cloud AutoML.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.240
These are just examples.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.550
The possibilities are
pretty much endless.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.100
Note that you can create
multiple projects,

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.600
all attached to
the billing account

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.670
that has the $300 credits.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.710
This could enable you
to try different things

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.210
in separate environments.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.090
As you explore GCP and
come across questions,

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.740
we have documentation
and community

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.440
forums to help guide
you, as well as

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.020
a free trial troubleshooter.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.270
If you have more
specific concerns that

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.600
require formal support, you can
purchase silver level support

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.940
using a portion of
your $300 credit

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.700
straight from the console
in the support section.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.420
This trial remains valid
for 12 months, or until you

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.710
use all of the $300.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.570
The amount of credit
and days remaining

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:36.260
are displayed at the top of the
Google Cloud Platform console,

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.310
as well as in the
billing section.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:42.670
If you do use all the credits,
you will not be charged,

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:44.680
but your resources
will be paused,

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.730
unless you upgrade to a
paid account within 30 days.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:51.190
You can upgrade to paid
account at any time,

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:54.010
and retain whatever's
left of the $300.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.170
Once you do this, you
become responsible

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:58.910
for the cost of
your GCP resources.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.630
Now let's talk
about the free tier.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.010
Once you've upgraded
to a paid account,

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:07.750
GCP still offers generous
free tiers for 16

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.280
of its main products.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.400
This is sometimes
referred to as free quota.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.970
These products include App
Engine, Compute Engine,

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:19.510
Kubernetes Engine, Cloud
Storage, Cloud Functions,

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.420
our Cloud Vision, Speech,
and Natural Language APIs,

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.220
and more.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:28.360
These free tiers allow GCP
users to use products for free

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.570
every month.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:32.380
For instance, the first
2 million invocations

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.900
of Cloud Functions
per month are free.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.710
And so are the first 60
minutes of Cloud Speech API,

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:43.690
or the first daily 120
build minutes of CloudBuild.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.450
Some of those services,
such as Compute Engine

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.370
or Cloud Storage,
will be required

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.680
to use specific GCP regions.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:54.220
As the name implies, Always
Free does not expire.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.920
If you'd like to find out
more about the free trial,

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.730
or the Always Free tier, check
out the detailed FAQ page.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:04.600
We hope that the combination of
the free trial, the Always Free

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.080
tier, and the simple GCP
pricing will enable you

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.450
to build amazing things on GCP.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.930
If you liked this video, please
like, subscribe, comment,

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:18.030
share, and look forward to
more GCP Essentials videos.

